/**
 * Client feedback patch (Nov 2026). Apply on top of the borrowed-faculty patch (166767b).
 *  1. Email: the field says what it is for, and the sign-in field takes the username OR the email
 *     ("login"; an "@" means email; emails are stored in lower case).
 *  2. Faculty page text is dark again; pale greys on the light pages are raised to a readable grey.
 *  3. Attendance Summary lists Male / Female / No gender set apart, like the Class Record.
 *  4. Attendance and grade items must be dated inside the term's cutoffs (server and date pickers), both ends included:
 *     attendance semester start..finals cutoff, midterm items start..midterm cutoff, finals items midterm cutoff+1..finals cutoff.
 *     Recording is CLOSED when the term has no academic period or the period lacks a date. "Today" is Asia/Manila.
 *     A grade item left without a date is dated today. New "Semester Start" on academic periods (editable).
 *  5. Borrowed teachers: classes are separated by department on My Subjects and My Classes; either Dean can Revoke
 *     an approved loan (blocked while the teacher still has current-semester classes from it).
 *  6. Academic periods: a semester has ended by its dates (so a past school year's 1st semester is refused like the 2nd);
 *     school year format, date order and the school-year span are validated; a period used by an active class term
 *     cannot be deleted; a period without all three dates cannot be made active.
 *  7. Advisers: the server now requires an active teacher of the department (borrowed teachers were only hidden in the dropdown).
 *  8. Plain-language instructions under the buttons (and in the confirm dialogs) of the screens this patch touches.
 * All-or-nothing: every edit is checked and applied in memory first; nothing is written unless all of them match
 * exactly once. Run from the project root:   php client-feedback-patch.php      then      php artisan migrate
 */
